Subject: cpu_engine: fix blending on transparent target pixels

Images and scenes blended with Multiply, Overlay, Darken and similar modes over transparent
target pixels applied the source alpha twice. The blender now gets an opaque, unpremultiplied
source and the result is interpolated by the source alpha once.

Origin: thorvg/thorvg PR #4884 "cpu_engine: fix blending on transparent target pixels"
by Shiny (@ShinyChang), https://github.com/thorvg/thorvg/pull/4884 (closed, not merged).
Ported by Lordicon to the current tvgSwRaster.cpp (after the SIMD refactor
rasterUnpremultiply() is UNPREMULTIPLY()); tests from the PR not included.
Upstream issue: https://github.com/thorvg/thorvg/issues/4893
Base: thorvg/thorvg main 72a66415 (1.2.0). License: MIT, like ThorVG.
---
diff --git a/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRaster.cpp b/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRaster.cpp
